      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "venir a + verbo en forma de diccionario",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that someone comes in order to do an activity?",
      "answerEn": "Use a form of venir, then a, then the action verb in its unchanged dictionary form.",
      "noteEn": "Venir changes for the person, time, or command: viene, vinieron, ven, and so on. The activity after a stays in its dictionary form ending in -ar, -er, or -ir. This lesson is about literal movement for a purpose; other figurative uses of venir a are separate.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Lucía viene a estudiar.",
        "en": "Lucía comes to study."
      },
      "tags": ["grammar", "movement", "purpose", "infinitive", "A1"]
    }
